 "title": "Volkswagen T1 Samba Bus (23-window, 1963) 1:16",
 "notes": "Body in two shells split at the belt moulding (upper blue-white, lower turquoise), as Revell splits its body; glaze the upper shell and the doors on the bench before they meet the chassis. Doors, cargo doors, engine lid and the four sunroof panels are separate, to hinge or slide. Wheels are built apart (tyre, rim, hubcap) and fitted to the drums. Mask the V on the nose in the upper colour. The engine block (crankcase, barrels, heads) is alloy with the barrels painted black; the shroud and accessories are a black piece. One canvas piece for the folded sunroof. Paint the swing-axle tubes and drums black over the alloy transaxle. Doors and cargo doors are two-tone: mask along the belt moulding (frames above it in L289). Belt and rocker trim in chrome foil. Engine: alloy block (barrels brushed black), black tinware, black carburettor and air cleaner, black exhaust. Transaxle alloy; swing-axle tubes with reduction boxes and drums black. v5 (2026-10-31): the fitted construct (fit round 1) and Revell-level detail; glazing after the roof. v7: the v6 kit critic's plan (V and side trims into the lower body, the roundel one piece, the sunroof one piece with its bows), door cards as separate pieces (Revell keeps them apart), mirror heads on their arms, the speedometer pod on the dash, sills reaching the side panels. v11: door cards merged into their doors (the tool hangs a moving group on the body; a card that touches only its door has no earlier host)."
